# DECISION RULE (fixed before the result), read from the all-companies rows by the assistant (z = (ratio - 1) / SE):
#   (a) L4_all day -4: 1.202 (SE 0.068, z 2.97) against 1.12: HOLDS.   (b) L4_all day -3: 1.154 (SE 0.044, z 3.50) against 1.12: HOLDS.
#   (c) L3_all day -2: 1.169 (SE 0.048, z 3.52) against 1.10: HOLDS.   (d) L2_all day -1: 1.270 (SE 0.059, z 4.58) against 1.20: HOLDS.
#   VERDICT: ROBUST (4 of 4 conditions; the rule asked for at least 3). The early-day reaction at lags 2 to 4 is not a neighbouring-event artifact; the description in the reaction-day profile result stands, and the lag-split result needs no extra check.
#   SAMPLE CHECK: the smallest group keeps 1,049 events (threshold 700).
# RETENTION: L2 1,251 of 1,355 (92.3 percent), L3 1,049 of 1,132 (92.7 percent), L4 1,082 of 1,204 (89.9 percent). CHANGE FROM THE EARLIER ISOLATION (earlier to wider): L4 day -4 1.210 to 1.202; L4 day -3 1.177 to 1.154; L3 day -2 1.171 to 1.169; L3 day -3 1.100 to 1.087 (now under 1.10, not a condition); L2 day -1 1.285 to 1.270; L2 day 0 1.272 to 1.270.
# CONSISTENCY (not independent confirmation; the sealed set was part of the profile result): all four tested bumps stay above 1.10 in the non-sealed and in the sealed set: L4 day -4 1.148 / 1.309; L4 day -3 1.172 / 1.118; L3 day -2 1.193 / 1.124; L2 day -1 1.323 / 1.173.

